 "answer_to_user": "I screened the Biotechnology sector (GICS 352010) in China, restricted to small/micro-cap size tiers and low-revenue (early-stage) — which cleanly excludes the mega-cap pharma (e.g. BeiGene, ~$60bn, is filtered out). 39 names matched, mostly pre-revenue clinical-stage biotechs listed in Hong Kong (.HK) and on the STAR/ChiNext boards (.CG). The larger of the small-caps:\n\n• InventisBio (688382.CG, ~$1.9bn) · Chongqing Genrix Biopharmaceutical (688443.CG, ~$1.4bn) · Ascletis Pharma (1672.HK, ~$1.4bn) · Tennor Therapeutics (6872.HK, ~$1.3bn) · CARsgen Therapeutics (2171.HK, ~$1.1bn)\n\nSmaller / earlier-stage: Shouyao Holdings (688197.CG), Xuanzhu Biopharm (2575.HK), Hinova Pharmaceuticals (688302.CG), TransThera Sciences (2617.HK), Jacobio Pharmaceuticals (1167.HK), Laekna (2105.HK), Clover Biopharmaceuticals (2197.HK), Antengene (6996.HK), TYK Medicines (2410.HK), Jiangsu Recbio (2179.HK).\n\nThese are genuine early-stage Chinese biotechs (most show no reported revenue yet / negative free cash flow — typical of clinical-stage names), not big pharma. Hong Kong's 18A-style listings dominate the list."
